**Question**: We can represent a set as a list of distinct elements, and we can represent the set of all subsets of the set as a list of lists. For example, if the set is `(1 2 3)`, then the set of all subsets is `(() (3) (2) (2 3) (1) (1 3) (1 2) (1 2 3))`. Complete the following definition of a procedure that generates the set of subsets of a set and give a clear explanation of why it works:

```scheme
(define (subsets s)
  (if (null? s)
      (list nil)
      (let ((rest (subsets (cdr s))))
        (append rest (map <??> rest)))))
```

